          "prompt_rule": "Three multi-part tasks from the chosen chapter, each with parts (a), (b) and (c) on one set of numbers (e.g. write the number in words, expand it, round it; or find the sum, the difference and compare). No two tasks test the same skill. Every part works on the task's own numbers; no part re-asks a Section A or B item. Answer: each part's working and result. Scheme: M 2 for the method, M 1 for the working, A 1 for the answer, U 1 for the unit or the statement. A common error names the figure its slip gives. No stem prescribes the method; the key pays any correct method. A check is a different method, never the commuted product; the three alternatives are equal in demand; a part never carries its own question label. Place-value wording is plain: say \"24 is 2 tens and 4 ones\", never \"24 ones groups\". A part asking for \"the number of ones\" says whether it means the digit in the ones place or the total in ones. A part asking for \"another multiplication sentence with the same total\" has an accept line saying any sentence with that total is right (the commuted form and other factor pairs), never one fixed sentence. No story or word problem: bare numbers and figures-free wording only.",
